# Build context filter for the fan-out snapshot.
#
# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, not `.dockerignore`: Docker only reads
# `.dockerignore` from the build context root, and this build's context is the
# repo root. BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile,
# which is what keeps this filter with the image that needs it.
#
# Every pattern is `**/`-prefixed on purpose. A bare `rom/` matches only the
# repo-root copy, and this repo carries git worktrees under .worktrees/ that
# each hold their own rom/ and .venv/ — without `**/`, a 3.2 GB image with
# three ROMs in it is the result.

# ROMs are never redistributed. This is the load-bearing rule.
**/rom/
**/*.gb
**/*.gbc
**/*.ram
**/*.sav
**/*.state

# Git worktrees: whole extra checkouts, each with deps and ROMs of its own.
**/.worktrees/

# Credentials — the image is built once and reused by every arm.
**/.env
**/*.key
**/api-key-*.txt

# Local run output, caches, and virtualenvs.
**/frames/
**/runs/
**/demo-runs/
**/pokedex/memory/
**/notes.md
**/notes.md.bak
**/.tapes/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/.git/
**/.DS_Store
